			"type": "text",
			"text": "Scanilepis is a ray finned fresh water fish that was discovered in Höganäs Formation of Sweden, dating back to the Triassic. The name is a mix of 'Scani' and 'lepis' meaning 'Scani fish', with Scania being the historic name of the region it was discovered in. It was a pretty big fish, estimated to be about 110 centimeters on average but an individual of a size estimated to be 2 meters has also been found. "
